Chapter: WhenBoolCross
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A cross-backend regression for Boolean and literal pattern dispatch.
 A `when` on a Boolean scrutinee reaches the plug as an IrLitPat whose
 value is the spelling `True` or `False`; the plug must read those as 1
 and 0. Reading them with a plain integer parse yields 0 for both and
 inverts the arms, so `frm` returned its initial accumulator (100)
 instead of 150. spin2/spin3/cross also pin the frameless and framed
 tail-call paths that were correct and must stay so.

Section: Loops

  spin2 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  spin2 (n) (acc) =
   if n == 0 then acc
   else let a = n - 1
    in let b = acc + 10
    in let c = a + 0
    in let d = b + 0
    in spin2 c d

  spin3 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  spin3 (n) (acc) (k) =
   if n == 0 then acc
   else let a = n - 1
    in let b = acc + 10
    in let c = a + 0
    in let d = b + 0
    in spin3 c d k

  cross : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  cross (n) (acc) =
   if n == 0 then acc
   else cross (n - 1) (acc + n)

  frm : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  frm (n) (acc) =
   when n == 0
    is True -> acc
    is False -> frm (n - 1) (acc + 10)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("spin2: " & show (spin2 5 100))
    print-line-uni ("spin3: " & show (spin3 5 100 0))
    print-line-uni ("cross: " & show (cross 5 100))
    print-line-uni ("frm: " & show (frm 5 100))
  end
